WEBVTT

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:07.140
Every sales team records its calls.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.140
Almost nobody listens to them.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.140
Managers review one call when something goes wrong,

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.140
then coach from memory,

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:18.140
so the same mistakes repeat across the team week after week.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.140
The rep who rushes discovery never finds out.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.140
The objection that gets dismissed never gets fixed.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.140
The call that ended with,

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.140
I'll follow up sometime,

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.140
never gets flagged.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:32.140
And when you hire someone new,

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:34.140
you have no baseline.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.140
Just a feeling that they're doing fine.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.140
The calls are already recorded.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:41.140
The coaching is the part that never happens.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.140
Worry not, I'm here to close your loop.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:46.140
Here's what happens after every call now.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.140
The call recording service

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:51.140
sends the finished call to the workflow

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.140
with the transcript attached.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.140
First, a check.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:56.140
Is there a usable transcript?

00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:00.140
If not, the call is skipped instead of scored badly.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:04.140
Then the AI scores the call against one fixed rubric.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.140
Opening, discovery, objection handling,

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.140
next step and compliance.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:12.140
Every score has to cite an exact quote from the transcript.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:15.140
Then the workflow checks the AI's work.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:18.140
It clamps the scores into range,

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.140
recomputes the overall score in code

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:22.140
instead of trusting the model

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.140
and verifies each quote

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.140
really appears in the transcript.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.140
Emails and phone numbers are redacted

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.140
before anything is stored.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:32.140
Clean calls go into a QA table.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:36.140
Risky calls or calls where the evidence was thin

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:39.140
also become a Gmail draft for a manager.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:43.140
And every Monday, one digest summarizes the week per rep

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.140
and files a single coaching draft.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:48.140
Nobody has to remember to review calls.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.140
The coaching finds you.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:53.140
Coach every call, not just the memorable ones.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.140
Bring a week of your team's calls

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.140
and I'll show you the pattern your managers are missing.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:01.140
I'm Christian, n8n automation architect.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.140
Book a discovery call now.
